lalalajpatrai","shimla"],"summary":"The statue depicts Lala Lajpat Rai, one of India's freedom fighters, addressing an audience and standing on a marble podium. It was originally erected in Lahore in 1929 but was moved to its current location in Shimla in 1948 after the partition of India.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Shimla","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Cityscape_of_Shimla.jpg/1280px-Cityscape_of_Shimla.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Cityscape_of_Shimla.jpg/500px-Cityscape_of_Shimla.jpg","w":1200,"h":744,"author":"Navneet Sharma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cityscape_of_Shimla.jpg"}},{"id":"shimla_wv_lower_bazaar","areaId":"shimla","name":"Lower Bazaar","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":31.10387,"lng":77.1749},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"shimla_wv_lower_bazaar","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":54,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["lowerbazaar","shimla"],"summary":"Shops open M-Sa. The Lower Bazaar is home to the city's less expensive hotels, cheaper restaurants and shops, and a congested wholesale vegetable market. Although less opulent than its upper neighbor, the Lower Bazaar retains an old worldly charm and is an excellent place to try some Shimla specialty dishes, like Uradh Dal with rice or Shepherd's Pie.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Shimla","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Christ_Church%2C_Shimla.jpg/1280px-Christ_Church%2C_Shimla.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Christ_Church%2C_Shimla.jpg/500px-Christ_Church%2C_Shimla.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"ShashankSharma2511","license":"CC BY 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedi